# UI Styling & Design System

## UI Library Stack
- **Primary**: MUI (Material-UI) - Main component library with SX-based styling
- **Styling**: MUI SX prop for all custom styling needs
- **No mixing** of other UI libraries or styling approaches

## MUI Design System

### MUI Component Usage
```javascript
// ✅ Correct - Use MUI components directly
import { 
  Button, 
  TextField, 
  Card, 
  CardContent,
  Typography,
  Box,
  Grid
} from '@mui/material'

const FundCard = ({ fund }) => {
  return (
    <Card sx={{ maxWidth: 345 }}>
      <CardContent>
        <Typography variant="h6" component="h2">
          {fund.name}
        </Typography>
        <Typography variant="body2" color="text.secondary">
          NAV: ₹{fund.nav}
        </Typography>
      </CardContent>
    </Card>
  )
}
```

### MUI Theme Configuration
```javascript
// src/theme/index.js
import { createTheme } from '@mui/material/styles'

const theme = createTheme({
  palette: {
    primary: {
      main: '#1976d2',
      light: '#42a5f5',
      dark: '#1565c0'
    },
    secondary: {
      main: '#dc004e'
    },
    success: {
      main: '#2e7d32'
    },
    error: {
      main: '#d32f2f'
    },
    warning: {
      main: '#ed6c02'
    }
  },
  typography: {
    fontFamily: '"Roboto", "Helvetica", "Arial", sans-serif',
    h4: {
      fontWeight: 600
    },
    h6: {
      fontWeight: 500
    }
  },
  spacing: 8, // 8px base spacing unit
  shape: {
    borderRadius: 8
  }
})

export default theme
```

### Custom MUI Components
Create reusable MUI wrappers in `src/components/common/`:

```javascript
// src/components/common/AppTextField.jsx
import React from 'react'
import { TextField } from '@mui/material'
import PropTypes from 'prop-types'

const AppTextField = ({
  label,
  value,
  onChange,
  error,
  helperText,
  required = false,
  type = 'text',
  ...props
}) => {
  return (
    <TextField
      label={label}
      value={value}
      onChange={onChange}
      error={!!error}
      helperText={error || helperText}
      required={required}
      type={type}
      variant="outlined"
      fullWidth
      margin="normal"
      {...props}
    />
  )
}

AppTextField.propTypes = {
  label: PropTypes.string.isRequired,
  value: PropTypes.string.isRequired,
  onChange: PropTypes.func.isRequired,
  error: PropTypes.string,
  helperText: PropTypes.string,
  required: PropTypes.bool,
  type: PropTypes.string
}

export default AppTextField
```

## MUI SX-Based Styling

### SX Prop Usage
Use MUI's SX prop for all custom styling needs:

```javascript
// ✅ Correct - SX-based styling
const FundList = () => {
  return (
    <Box
      sx={{
        display: 'grid',
        gridTemplateColumns: {
          xs: '1fr',
          md: 'repeat(2, 1fr)',
          lg: 'repeat(3, 1fr)'
        },
        gap: 2,
        p: 2
      }}
    >
      {funds.map(fund => (
        <Card
          key={fund.id}
          sx={{
            bgcolor: 'white',
            borderRadius: 2,
            boxShadow: 2,
            p: 2,
            transition: 'all 0.2s ease-in-out',
            '&:hover': {
              boxShadow: 4,
              transform: 'translateY(-2px)'
            }
          }}
        >
          <Typography variant="h6" sx={{ fontWeight: 600, color: 'grey.800' }}>
            {fund.name}
          </Typography>
          <Typography variant="body2" sx={{ color: 'grey.600' }}>
            {fund.category}
          </Typography>
        </Card>
      ))}
    </Box>
  )
}
```

